**Who they are:** Nail-trend-aware women, mid-20s to late-30s, active on Pinterest/TikTok/Instagram, already comfortable booking creative manicures — browsing for their next appointment, not nail-tech beginners.

**What they want:** A curated, identity-sorted set of bangle nail looks they can screenshot and take to a salon, plus reassurance on cost/time/durability and whether an at-home version is realistic.

**What frustrates them:** Existing coverage is either a thin photo dump with no guidance (Bustle) or a gorgeous-but-overwhelming maximalist gallery with no "which one is me" filter. Nobody addresses short nails or DIY viability head-on.

**Top 5 pain points:**
1. Not knowing which words to use with a nail tech to get the 3D "bangle" effect rather than flat nail art
2. Fear the look only works on long/acrylic nails, not natural short nails
3. Uncertainty whether this is realistically DIY-able or an automatic salon trip
4. Not knowing which metal tone (gold vs. silver vs. chrome) suits their skin tone or existing jewelry
5. Wanting the look for a specific event/season but not knowing which version reads "everyday" vs. "special occasion"

